  "project_title": "Microbial community dynamics during anaerobic digestion of high-ammonia livestock wastewater under different aeration pretreatments",
  "project_description": "This BioProject contains Illumina 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing data generated to characterize bacterial and archaeal community dynamics during anaerobic digestion of high-ammonia livestock wastewater.</p><p>Three pretreatment strategies were investigated, including nanobubble aeration pretreatment, conventional aeration pretreatment, and non-aerated control. Samples were collected from anaerobic digestion systems at different incubation stages.</p><p>The V3-V4 region of bacterial 16S rRNA genes and archaeal 16S rRNA genes were amplified and sequenced separately. Sequencing data were used to investigate microbial succession, nitrogen transformation-related microorganisms, methanogenic archaea, and their relationships with methane production performance during anaerobic digestion.</p><p>This dataset provides raw sequencing reads for studying microbial mechanisms involved in anaerobic treatment of livestock wastewater under different aeration strategies.",
